describe('The Interceptor', () => {
  it('intercepts the API and injects custom data', () => {
    cy.visit('/pages/level-08/');
    // Hint: wait for a request or timeout
    // Hint: use cy.get()
  });
});

solution:
describe('The Interceptor', () => {
  it('intercepts the API and injects custom data', () => {
      cy.intercept('GET', '/api/items', {
        body: { items: ['dragon-scale', 'fire-gem'] }
      }).as('getItems');
      cy.visit('/pages/level-08/');
      cy.wait('@getItems');
      cy.get('.item-entry').should('contain', 'dragon-scale');
    });
});

explanation:
`cy.intercept(method, url, response)` intercepts network requests — Cypress's equivalent of `page.route()`.

```
cy.intercept('GET', '/api/items', [{ name: 'dragon-scale' }]).as('getItems');
cy.visit('/pages/level-08/');
cy.wait('@getItems');
cy.contains('dragon-scale').should('be.visible');
```

Unlike Playwright routes, `cy.intercept()` can be set up at any point — not just before `cy.visit()`.

