describe('The Shadow Realm', () => {
  it('accesses shadow DOM with .shadow()', () => {
    cy.visit('/pages/level-85/');
    cy.get('#spell-host').shadow().find('#shadow-spell-name').should('contain', 'Fireball');
  });
});

explanation:
`.shadow()` pierces the shadow boundary of a custom element and lets you query inside it with normal `cy.get()` / `.find()`.

```
cy.get('#spell-host').shadow().find('#shadow-spell-name')
  .should('contain', 'Fireball');
// nested shadow DOM
cy.get('#nested-host').shadow().find('#inner-host').shadow()
  .find('#shadow-inner-text').should('contain', 'ARCANE_KEY');
```

Alternatively set `includeShadowDom: true` in `cypress.config.js` to pierce all shadow roots globally.

